From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SRNet <121732083+SRNet-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Exit ranges: guard with shared_mutex

RPC MapExit/UnmapExit/SwapExits (OMQ thread) mutate exit ranges while the
packet path (TUN thread) reads them. Writers now take
Router::exit_ranges_mutex() exclusively; exit_for_ip, remote_is_exit_broker,
on_connected and ListExits take it shared (ListExits copies a snapshot).
No routing/session calls are made under the exclusive lock.
---
 src/handlers/tun.cpp   |  7 +++++-
 src/router/router.hpp  | 12 ++++++++++
 src/rpc/rpc_server.cpp | 54 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 3 files changed, 55 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/handlers/tun.cpp b/src/handlers/tun.cpp
index 5544004..0efe6cd 100644
--- a/src/handlers/tun.cpp
+++ b/src/handlers/tun.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@
 #include <oxenc/endian.h>
 
 #include <chrono>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <shared_mutex>
 #include <span>
 #include <variant>
 #ifndef _WIN32
@@ -140,7 +142,7 @@ namespace srouter::handlers
